<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Somali Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1960 CE – 1969 CE · capital Mogadishu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first independent Somali state, formed by uniting the former British and Italian territories in 1960, and a parliamentary democracy until 1969.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 1 July 1960 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-somaliland">State of Somaliland</a>, independent for five days, united with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trust-territory-of-somaliland">Trust Territory of Somaliland</a> to form the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> Republic, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-mogadishu">Mogadishu</a> as capital. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden-abdullah-osman">Aden Abdullah Osman</a> became provisional president and the constitution was approved by referendum in 1961, though many northerners voted against it.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic was a multi-party parliamentary democracy, among the more open in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, but politics was dominated by clan rivalries and patronage. It pursued the goal of uniting all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somalis</a> in a Greater <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/somalia">Somalia</a>, supporting insurgents in Kenya's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-frontier-district">Northern Frontier District</a>, the Shifta War, and fighting a border war with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federal-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> in 1964. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdirashid-ali-shermarke">Abdirashid Ali Shermarke</a> won the presidency in 1967.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 15 October 1969 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdirashid-ali-shermarke">Shermarke</a> was assassinated, and six days later the army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siad-barre">Mohamed Siad Barre</a> seized power, dissolving parliament and creating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/somali-democratic-republic">Somali Democratic Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/somali-republic.jpg" alt="Somali Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: see upload history · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Somalia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1960 CE – 1969 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mogadishu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Aden Abdullah Osman, Abdirashid Ali Shermarke, Muhammad Haji Ibrahim Egal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Somali, Italian, English, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/somalia">Somalia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Somalia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1964&amp;focus=somali-republic" aria-label="Somali Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5939 2101 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Somali Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6259 2357L6259 2357M6259 2357L6216 2076M6259 2357L6259 2357"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6259 2357h0M6216 2076h0M6259 2357h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6259 2357h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6259 2357h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mogadishu. <a href="/atlas?year=1964&amp;focus=somali-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
